{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggDEZJTcCNBAfwGRzwog","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed it: `split_cents(100, 3)` now returns `[34, 33, 33]`, so no grosz goes missing.\n\n**The bug:** `split_cents` gave everyone `total // people` and threw away the remainder.\n\n**The fix** (`money.py`): it now uses `divmod` to get both the share and the remainder, and gives the leftover grosze one each to the first people in the list. The shares always add up to the total, and no two shares differ by more than 1 grosz.\n\n**Tests** (`test_money.py`): I added two tests:\n- A check that the 1 zł / 3 people case returns exactly `[34, 33, 33]`.\n- A check over every total from 0 to 249 grosze and 1 to 7 people that the shares add up to the total and differ by at most 1.\n\nBoth failed before the fix. Now all 5 tests pass.\n\nThe extra grosz always goes to whoever is first in the list. If you'd rather it go to someone else, like the person who paid, that's a small change."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":543,"cache_read_input_tokens":19208,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":543},"output_tokens":324,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3c3ba56a-749f-4d77-b80c-b2bf5980fe12","uuid":"ca447b22-ba3d-4c39-ac9c-3c2514b041e6","timestamp":"2026-11-03T15:13:32.818Z","request_id":"req_011CggDEYzrFJohN1dhGbnmS"}
